-- title:
--   Deuring: Frobenius kernel ideal is the prime above q'
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic a prime $q'$, and let $X_0$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$ all of whose affine points $P$ with $q' \cdot P = 0$ vanish. Let $a, b \in \mathbb{Q}$ be such that $a < 0$, $b < 0$ and, for every height-one prime $v$ of the ring of integers of $\mathbb{Q}$, the algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b] \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ has all nonzero elements invertible exactly when $q'$ lies in $v$. Let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ containing $1$, closed under multiplication, finitely generated, spanning the algebra over $\mathbb{Q}$, and maximal among submodules with these properties; and let $\theta$ be an injective ring homomorphism from [`WeierstrassCurve.rationalEndSubring κ X₀`](def/WeierstrassCurve_RationalEnd.html#L32) — the subring of additive endomorphisms of the group of affine points generated by the maps that are zero or rationally represented — onto $\Lambda$ as a set. Then $\theta$ carries the set of those endomorphisms that factor as the $q'$-power point map $(x,y) \mapsto (x^{q'}, y^{q'})$ into the twist `X₀.map (frobenius κ q')` followed by some rationally represented (or zero) homomorphism back to $X_0$, precisely onto the set of $h \in \Lambda$ with $h = 0$ or $\mathrm{padicValRat}\,q'(\mathrm{nrd}\,h) \ge 1$, where $\mathrm{nrd}\,h = h_{\mathrm{re}}^2 - a\,h_{i}^2 - b\,h_{j}^2 + ab\,h_{k}^2$.
--
--   This is Deuring's description of the two-sided prime above $q'$ in the endomorphism ring of a supersingular elliptic curve: the inseparable endomorphisms, namely those factoring through the $q'$-power Frobenius, are exactly the elements of reduced norm divisible by $q'$. It feeds the computation of the kernel ideal of a Frobenius-twisted isogeny in [`CerednikDrinfeld.image_kernelIdealSet_ratPointHom_frobenius_comp_eq_star_smul_ofFiniteIdele_mul`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.image_kernelIdealSet_ratPointHom_frobenius_comp_eq_star_smul_ofFiniteIdele_mul).
